'''CR4ZY''' ''(formerly known as '''Valiance & Co''')'' is a [[:Category:Croatia|Croatian]] esports organization.

==Timeline==
{{Tabs dynamic
|name1=2017
|name2=2018
|name3=2019
|name4=2020
|This=4

|content1=
*October 21st - '''Valiance''' acquire [[Binary Dragons]]' ''[[Counter-Strike: Global Offensive|Global Offensive]]'' team. <ref name="BD to Valiance">{{cite web|url=https://www.hltv.org/news/21818/valiance-sign-binary-dragons|title=Valiance sign Binary Dragons"|date=2017-10-21|author=[[Professeur]]|publisher=[[HLTV]]}}</ref>

|content2=
*March 1st - [[soLo]] leaves '''Valiance'''. <ref name="-soLo">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/solitoCSGO/status/969230098774683648|title=Hello everyone! I'm not a part of @valianceandco anymore, and I am open for offers|date=2018-03-01|author=[[soLo]]}}</ref>
*March 12th - [[Impulse]] replaces [[DJOXiC]]. <ref name="-DJOXiC +Impulse">{{cite web|url=https://www.hltv.org/news/23026/valiance-replace-djoxic-with-impulse|title=Valiance replace DJOXiC with Impulse|date=2018-03-12|author=[[Benja]]|publisher=[[HLTV]]}}</ref>
*June 13th - '''Valiance''' add [[kassad]] as coach. <ref name="+kassad">{{cite web|url=https://www.hltv.org/news/23944/kassad-joins-valiance-as-coach|title=Kassad joins Valiance as coach|date=2018-06-13|author=[[MIRAA]]|publisher=[[HLTV]]}}</ref>
*August 14th - '''Valiance''' replace [[NENO]] with [[jayzaR]]. <ref name="-NENO +jayzaR">{{cite web|url=https://www.valiance.gg/news/jayzar-joins-valiance-co-csgo-team?tags=homepage|title=Valiance have announced the release of Anel "NENO" Ceković and the addition of former Chaos player Aleksandar "jayzaR" Zarkovic|date=2018-08-14|publisher='''Valiance'''}}</ref>
*October 8th - [[kassad]] is re-signed by [[Renegades]] as their coach. <ref name="-kassad">{{cite web|url=https://www.hltv.org/news/25026/azr-bringing-kassad-back-is-a-permanent-thing|date=2018-10-08|title=AZR: "Bringing kassad back is a permanent thing"|author=[[LucasAM]]|publisher=[[HLTV]]}}</ref>
*November 3rd - '''Valiance''' sign [[nexa]], [[EspiranTo]] and [[ottoNd]], bench [[jayzaR]] and [[Impulse]], finally [[emi]] moves to an analyst position. <ref name="Nov 2018">{{cite web|url=https://www.valiance.gg/news/roster-update-for-valiance-co-csgo-team|title=Roster update for Valiance&CO CS:GO team|date=2018-11-03|publisher='''Valiance'''}}</ref>
*November 14th - [[jayzaR]] announced that his contract with the organization had ended. <ref name="-jayzaR">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/jayzaRCSGO/status/1062668315431190528|title=Officially out of my contract as it ends today :) Ready for new adventures.. looking for a new home|date=2018-11-14|author=[[jayzaR]]}}</ref>

|content3=
*January 1st - [[Impulse]]'s contract expires. <ref name="-Impulse">{{inside source|date=2019-01-01|lp-date=2019-02-08|source=Impulse|source-role=Player|lp-source=Omarion}}</ref>
*February 7th - [[DJOXiC]] is acquired by [[Entity Gaming]]. <ref name="-DJOXiC">{{cite web|url=https://www.facebook.com/notes/entity-gaming/cs-go-roster-update/2189811857903194|title=CS GO : ROSTER UPDATE|date=2019-02-07|author=[[Entity Gaming]]}}</ref>
*June 9th - '''Valiance & Co''' rebrand as '''CR4ZY'''. <ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/gocr4zy/status/1137658814864535552|title=It's time to @gocr4zy|date=2019-06-09|author='''CR4ZY'''}}</ref>
*September 30th - [[nexa]] and [[huNter-]] are acquired by [[G2 Esports]]. <ref name="-nexa -hNt">{{cite web|url=https://www.g2esports.com/g2-csgo-goes-global/|title=G2 CS:GO Goes Global|date=2019-09-30|author=[[Tina Sang]]|publisher=[[G2 Esports]]}}</ref>
*October 4th - '''CR4ZY''' sign [[SHiPZ]], [[emi]] returns to the active roster and [[NeiL_M]] joins as the team<nowiki>'s</nowiki> coach. <ref name="Oct 2019">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/gocr4zy/status/1180181914822553600|title=What do you think about our new roster?|date=2019-10-04|publisher='''CR4ZY'''}}</ref>

|content4=
*January 20th - '''CR4ZY'''<nowiki>'s</nowiki> lineup is acquired by [[c0ntact Gaming]]. <ref name="c0ntact">{{cite web|url=https://www.hltv.org/news/28876/cr4zy-transfer-roster-to-c0ntact-gaming|title=CR4ZY transfer roster to c0ntact Gaming|date=2020-01-20|author=[[Striker (Czech journalist)|Striker]]|publisher=[[HLTV]]}}</ref>
*February 18th - '''CR4ZY''' sign [[Project X]], a squad consisting of [[dERZKIY]], [[dOBRIY]], [[Sergiz]], [[Psycho]], [[SENSEi]] and [[Johnta]] - the latter as the team's coach. <ref name="Project X">{{cite web|url=https://cr4zy.gg/young-and-promising-cis-roster-led-by-veteran-ivan-johnta-shevtsov-to-represent-cr4zy/|title=New CS:GO Roster Led by Veteran Johnta|date=2020-02-18|publisher='''CR4ZY'''}}</ref>
*April 16th - '''CR4ZY''' bench [[dERZKIY]] and [[dOBRIY]]; they sign [[DemQQ]] and [[7oX1C]] as replacements. <ref name="April 2020">{{cite web|url=https://cr4zy.gg/cr4zy-csgo-welcoms-demqq-7ox1c/|title=Changes in the CR4ZY CS:GO|date=2020-04-16|publisher='''CR4ZY'''}}</ref>
*May 18th - [[dERZKIY]] joins [[Moscow Five Academy]] as a stand-in. <ref name="dERZKIY M5A">{{cite web|url=https://vk.com/wall-183160651_7789|title=Место rommi в команде займет dERZKIY, который на данном этапе выступает в роли stand-in|trans_title=Rommi's place in the team will be taken by dERZKIY, who at this stage acts as a stand-in|language={{Flag|ru}} Russian|author=[[Moscow Five Academy]]|date=2020-05-18}}</ref>
*May 21st - [[dOBRIY]] and [[dERZKIY]] are released from their contracts; they leave '''CR4ZY''' as a result. <ref name="-dOBRIY">{{cite web|url=https://vk.com/wall-28716563_21732|title=У меня нет контракта c СR4ZY, я свободный агент|trans_title=I don't have a contract with CR4ZY, I'm a free agent|language={{Flag|ru}} Russian|author=[[dOBRIY]]|date=2020-05-21}}</ref><ref name="-dERZKIY">{{inside source|date=2020-05-21|lp-date=2020-05-21|source=Johnta|source-role=CR4ZY coach|lp=source=Johnta}}</ref>
*September 30th - '''CR4ZY''' release their team. <ref name="CR4ZY disband 2020">{{cite web|url=https://cr4zy.gg/future-of-cr4zy-time-to-focus-on-2021|title=
Future of CR4ZY: Time to focus on 2021|publisher='''CR4ZY'''|date=2020-10-05}}</ref>
}}

